Here are four distinct global CSS themes you can drop directly into your `globals.css` file to instantly change the look of your entire site.

### Option 1: Midnight & Cyan (Modern Tech)

A sleek, high-contrast palette perfect for SaaS, tech, and modern digital agencies.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@layer base {
  :root {
    --bg-primary: #F8FAFC;      /* Slate 50 */
    --text-primary: #0F172A;    /* Slate 900 */
    --text-body: #334155;       /* Slate 700 */
    --card-bg: #FFFFFF;         /* Pure White */
    --border-color: #E2E8F0;    /* Slate 200 */
    --accent-action: #0284C7;   /* Bright Ocean Blue */
  }

  .dark {
    --bg-primary: #0F172A;      /* Slate 900 */
    --text-primary: #F8FAFC;    /* Slate 50 */
    --text-body: #CBD5E1;       /* Slate 300 */
    --card-bg: #1E293B;         /* Slate 800 */
    --border-color: #334155;    /* Slate 700 */
    --accent-action: #38BDF8;   /* Electric Cyan */
  }
}

body {
  background-color: var(--bg-primary);
  color: var(--text-body);
  font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
  transition: background-color 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
}

h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  color: var(--text-primary);
}

```

